+# U3 planning review evidence
+
+The installed `ce-plan` and `ce-doc-review` workflows ran using skill-local persona prompts, the documented generic-subagent template and findings schema. Two research delegates investigated current repository patterns and the declared solutions corpus. Packs resolved empty. No directly relevant institutional learning or external research dependency was found.
+
+Requirements were reviewed against the scoped user request, PRD and approved master plan before the canonical repository plan was authored. An initial unreviewed draft was moved to scratch before this checkpoint; no production work occurred. Six separate read-only contexts reviewed requirements; six new contexts reviewed the resulting plan. Each wave selected coherence, feasibility, design, security, scope and adversarial lenses. Product lens was not selected because this bounded U3 scope is already established by the user and approved upstream plan. All raw returns were valid and clean. The lead checked source references, scope, exact-decimal and validation semantics, execution ordering and test coverage. No corrections or user decisions remained.
+
+Confidence check passed without deepening. The plan includes typed constant/type constraints, honest constant provenance, minimal completed-card treatment, existing revision-safe scheduling and independent byte goldens. No code changes, dependency installation or tests were run by the planning agent.
+
+Cross-model discovery found only `/opt/codex/bin/codex`; no Claude, Grok, Cursor or OpenCode route was installed. The external pass did not run, no job started and no document content left the machine. The independently dispatched local adversarial lens completed in both waves; it is not a different-provider review.
+
+The raw and resolved JSON files retain exact reviewer responses and disposition. Temporary prompt/research files remain at `/tmp/ce-u3-plan-research` for the current session; they are not product artifacts.
